                        <origin><origDate calendar="#Gregorian" notBefore="1200" notAfter="1499">s.
                                xiii and xv</origDate></origin>
                        <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_189">Durham, Benedictine
                                cathedral priory of St Cuthbert</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the first edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1941). However, the attribution was
                                later accepted in the second edition (1964). There were no relevant
                                changes to this attribution in the Supplement (1987), at which point
                                Durham was entirely revisited by A. J. Piper. The attribution
                                appears to have been inadvertently omitted from MLGB3 (2010-2015).
                                The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card is
                                outdated, and corresponds to the original rejection. The card shows
                                that there were initially doubts about whether the pressmark, O/ii,
                                was connected with Durham. For comparison, MS 48 was listed
                                positively with this Durham pressmark in both the second edition
                                (1964) and the Supplement (1987).</p>
                            <q type="pressmark">O/ii</q></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Jesus College by <persName
                                role="fmo">Man</persName>.</provenance>
                    </history>
